113	     * > 2. `php tools/seed-insert.php`   — inserts seed data
114	     * >
115	     * > This method is retained as a programmatic entry point for callers that
116	     * > need to trigger truncation + seeding in a single in-process call
117	     * > (e.g. application-level Composer scripts that call `doSeedTests()`
